===Etymology===
{{unc|sa}}. Possibly a formation like {{m|sa|उपा॑क|t=brought near to each other, joined}}, with a cognate of {{cog|sla-pro|*na|t=on|id=auf}} as first element.<ref>{{R:EWAia|vol=II|page=33}}</ref>

The traditional explanation as {{com|sa|न|tr1=ná|t1=no|अक॑|tr2=áka|t2=sin, pain|lit=where there is no pain or sin}},<ref>{{R:MW|532|col=3}}</ref> is unlikely as the prefix {{m|sa|अ-}} ({{m|sa|अन्-}} before vowels) would rather have been used.

===Pronunciation===
{{sa-IPA|a=1}}

===Noun===
{{sa-noun|m|tr=nā́ka}}

# [[heaven]], [[firmament]]
#: {{syn|sa|Thesaurus:स्वर्ग}}
